        "bhavartha": "The poet calls Śiva by name after name: beloved of Śivā, Śambhu, the Lord crowned with a crescent moon, the great Lord who holds the trident and wears His matted hair in a coil. Then he says who this is: the One who spreads through the whole world, whose form is the universe. He ends by begging, twice, that this Lord, whole in form, be gracious."
      },
